# 1. Canonical domain.
# REMOVED 2026-09-02: this rule sent apex -> www, but the Cloudflare zone
# already 301s www -> apex, and zone rules run before Pages. Two rules pointing
# at each other is a redirect loop waiting to fire. Reality today is that the
# APEX serves the site and www redirects to it, so this rule was both dead and
# dangerous. Do not re-add a domain redirect here; set the direction once, at
# the zone level, and leave this file out of it.

# 2. Pretty-URL rewrites for marketing pages (clean, no .html)
# NOTE: only list ALIASES here — pages whose source filename differs from the URL.
# Pages handles /foo → /foo.html automatically when the filename matches the URL.
# Adding a redundant rule for those collides with Pages' built-in clean-URL handler
# and can cause loops. Only /free-map is a true alias to a different filename.
# NOTE: do not add rules here to hide internal files. Pages serves a matching
# static asset before consulting _redirects, so such rules never fire, and
# adding them broke /api/* Functions routing (verified 2026-09-02).
# Internal files are excluded at deploy time instead — see the deploy command
# in the project notes: deploy from an rsync'd copy that drops *.md and .claude.

# Retired coach products -> the one live coach product (2026-09-02).
# These only fire because deploy.sh keeps the matching .html out of the
# upload. Pages serves a static asset before reading this file, so if the
# page is ever re-published the redirect goes dead without warning.
/brand-os            /coach-platform           301
/build-your-brand    /coach-platform           301
/brand-os-session    /coach-platform           301
/augmented-coach     /coach-platform           301
/content-os          /coach-platform           301
/growth-engine       /coach-platform           301
/lead-os             /coach-platform           301

/free-map            /your-map.html            200

# Ops vertical (Aug 2026). /ops-audit was folded into the behavioral-health
# landing page so the offer and the proof live on one page for outbound.
/ops-audit           /behavioral-health        301
/billing-census      /behavioral-health        301

# 3. Portal pretty-URLs (auth-gated in the browser via Supabase)
